   "final_text": "The feed had six events: five manager changes and one termination. All six are done and checked. I've watched the feed for about an hour since, and no new events have come in.\n\n**Jordan Carter's termination (E1001, case-e1a5dbb0, effective today, 2026-11-02)**\n- **Access removed first:** I disabled Jordan's account (acct-e8624fab) and signed out the one active session.\n- **Mailbox kept:** It's now a shared mailbox, so the data is still there. There's no legal hold on Jordan, but nothing was deleted.\n- **Access groups and licenses:** I removed Jordan from all four groups (All-Staff, Eng-Git, Eng-Prod-Deploy, VPN-Users) and took off the Office-E3 license.\n- **Equipment:** Jordan has an engineering laptop bundle on record, so I opened a ticket to get it back (tkt-6b031f3d).\n- **Finance:** Jordan had no open expense reports of their own. Once access was removed, I deactivated the corporate card and requested final pay. Both of these can't be undone.\n\n**Moving five people from Jordan to Owen Iyer (E1009, effective 2026-11-01)**\n- **Future expenses:** All five now go to Owen for expense approval. Jordan no longer approves for anyone.\n- **Reports already waiting:** Changing the approver doesn't move reports that were already submitted, so I sent these four to Owen one by one:\n  - exp-2c70501e, $599\n  - exp-2e87d415, $988\n  - exp-scn-C5001, $640\n  - exp-e8147dc9, $900\n- **Checked afterwards:** When I re-read them, all four were still assigned to Owen.\n\nNothing failed, I didn't need to ask any team for a fix or escalate to a person, and nothing is still pending.\n\nOne thing you may want to check: Owen is a Sales Manager, and these five people were on an Engineering Manager's team. Workday names him as their new manager, so I followed that. He now approves expenses for eight people in total."
